"},"comments":11,"created_at":"2025-06-03T19:16:38Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T10:45:57Z","closed_at":"2025-09-22T13:56:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107096","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107096","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107096.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107096.patch","merged_at":"2025-09-22T13:56:28Z"},"body":"Closes #87747\r\n~~Requires libdecor=no to work and~~ Requires a compositor which supports it. As of this commit only KWin supports this protocol.\r\n\r\n~~Really not sure when libdecor actually sets the xdg_toplevel so with it enabled I couldn't get it to work but I can confirm that without libdecor on KWin this does work~~\r\n![Screenshot_20250603_195429](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/355f59b4-c7f4-4fe6-a5c0-d4fe22df56a1)\r\n\r\nWorks with project icons too\r\n![Screenshot_20250603_201132](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a8f9dee-a3c3-41c6-9b30-b8ecb2e949e5)\r\n\r\nAdding a name to the icon is for icon themes, if a system theme has an icon called \"godot\" it will be used instead of whatever godot actually submits in the buffer (I'm guessing a bit here, I don't know of an icon theme that themes godot so I haven't tested. That also means there's a bug where the running app will get themed like it's the godot editor but not sure what the icon name should be in that case)\r\n\r\nUPD 1: added libdecor=yes support","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/foll